    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. kept_work_guard.py:186-187 yields mutate for any AugAssign on a module container name, with no local-rebinding or global check (unlike :192, :197, :203). Without `global`, `|=` makes the name local (running it raises UnboundLocalError); with `global` the guard's global check catches it first. So every hit of this branch is a false positive that would force a bogus exemption. Repro: `_C = {}` then `def f(): _C = {}; _C |= {1: 2}` gives `mutate _C`. r30, v11."  # c14a
